That’s a different orientation from needing constant dominance.

It’s more like reserve capacity: you don’t have to prove maximum performance all the time because you trust that you can access a higher gear when the situation actually warrants it.

The useful distinction is:

\text{identity = “I must be the best”}

versus

\text{capability = “I can become extremely competitive when needed”}

The first can trap you in comparison. The second preserves flexibility.

And it fits the blade idea from earlier: the point is not to swing it constantly. The point is to know you can draw it, use it well, and put it away again.